# One per builder kind, and the half worth pinning is that the advice is still per-type: each names
# its own readers, recovered from the appender in the loop body, where keying on the call alone
# could only have given one vague message for all four.
lint 12:9 'snapshot' converts the whole of 'seen' on every pass of this loop, and the loop keeps adding to it (quadratic); read it in place with len, ab_get or 'for x in <the builder>'
lint 25:9 read it in place with len, mapb_get, mapb_get_or or mapb_contains
lint 36:9 read it in place with len, or a MutableString you finish once after the loop
lint 47:9 read it in place with len or setb_contains
